<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conquest of Larsa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1762 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century-bce">18th century BCE</a> · Also known as Hammurabi's conquest of Larsa, Larsa subdued</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/larsa">Larsa</a> was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a>'s capture of the rival southern Mesopotamian kingdom of Larsa, ruled by Rim-Sin, in 1762 BCE. Larsa had been one of the leading powers of the region. Its fall was a decisive step in transforming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> from one of several city-states into the Babylonian Empire.</p></div>
